{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>A double portion of bread.</b> From the implication of what is said, 'a double portion of bread,' I already know that it is two omers. So what does Scripture mean to tell by <b>two omers for one</b>? Two omers for the designated day, which is the Sabbath. Therefore the lamed has a qamatz — <b>for one</b>, meaning the designated, distinguished one." "<b>And they told Moses.</b> They were afraid to keep it hidden until the next day, because Moses had already become angry at those who left over. And he had not told them the matter of an omer on the Sabbath, so that each one would not gather only a single omer and it would amount to two."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:58:13.543240669Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}